  levelId: level_21
  levelTitle: Capacitor Charge - Store the Energy
  initialPage: 0
  pages:
  - title: LEVEL 21 | Capacitor Charging | Overview
    explanation: A capacitor stores energy in an electric field. With SW1 closed,
      it charges through the 1 kOhm resistor. The LCD is only a high-impedance voltmeter
      across capacitor terminals; it is not the return wire.
    caption: PAGE 1/4 | 5 V | R 1 kOhm | C 1000 uF
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.12, y: 0.5}
      label: 5 V
      color: {r: 0.99, g: 0.3, b: 0.4, a: 1}
    - id: switch
      kind: 5
      position: {x: 0.29, y: 0.8}
      label: SW1
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.79, b: 0.32, a: 1}
    - id: resistor
      kind: 1
      position: {x: 0.49, y: 0.8}
      label: R 1 kOhm
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.79, b: 0.32, a: 1}
    - id: capacitor
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.76, y: 0.55}
      label: C 1000 uF
      color: {r: 0.28, g: 0.95, b: 0.98, a: 1}
    - id: lcd
      kind: 8
      position: {x: 0.54, y: 0.36}
      label: LCD Vcap
      color: {r: 0.28, g: 0.95, b: 0.98, a: 1}
    - id: ground
      kind: 6
      position: {x: 0.46, y: 0.15}
      label: GND
      color: {r: 0.21, g: 0.7, b: 1, a: 1}
